<%= header_section(@subject) %>
<div>
  <p>
    Your <%= @resource_subscription.resource_name %> webhook<%= " for #{@application_name}" if @application_name.present? %>
    is still listed as active, but we are not able to send anything to it, so you are not receiving
    notifications for these events.
  </p>
  <% if @missing_post_url %>
    <p>
      The webhook does not have a URL to send to. Set one through the application that created it and
      we will start sending <%= @resource_subscription.resource_name %> notifications from your next
      sale onwards.
    </p>
  <% else %>
    <p>
      The application that created this webhook no longer has permission to read your sales, which is
      required for us to send it. Reconnecting Gumroad inside that application will restore the
      permission, and <%= @resource_subscription.resource_name %> notifications will resume from your
      next sale onwards. If you did not expect to hear from it, you can ignore this — nothing else is
      affected.
    </p>
  <% end %>
  <p>
    Webhooks like this one are created by the applications you connect, so there is nothing to change
    in your Gumroad settings. If you would rather send these notifications to your own URL instead,
    you can set one under <%= link_to "advanced settings", settings_advanced_url %>. Our
    <%= link_to "ping documentation", ping_url %> explains how they work.
  </p>
  <p>
    Reply to this email if you would like us to remove the webhook for you.
  </p>
</div>
